{
  "info": {
    "name": "IAM Service — Groups API",
    "_postman_id": "f6d4b8a3-1e5c-4a2f-9d3e-iam-groups-0001",
    "description": "Exercises every /api/v1/groups endpoint in app/api/v1/routes/groups.py, implemented from groups-group-memberships-api-spec. Sibling to ../group-memberships (the other half of that same spec doc, kept as its own collection so it can bootstrap an independent tenant), and to ../auth, ../users, ../tenants, ../roles, ../permissions.\n\n**Example data is drawn from scripts/dummy.json's Apple Corp tenant** (a realistic department/group layout) rather than generic placeholders — every group/user below corresponds to an entry there, *except* the platform superuser: dummy.json has no superadmin concept at all, and every Groups request in this collection is driven by the tenant **owner** (John Smith, CEO), never by `superuser_access_token` — creating/managing groups only ever requires being that tenant's owner. The platform superuser is used strictly for the one thing only it can do: bootstrapping the organization itself in Setup (same constraint every sibling collection works around).\n\n**Notes on the implementation vs. the spec doc:**\n- A group always belongs to exactly one tenant — unlike Role/Permission there is no global/platform group.\n- `tenant_id` in requests/responses is the organization's *slug* (e.g. `apple-corp`), not its internal id — same convention as every other resource in this service.\n- The response is a superset of the spec's own (truncated) example: it also includes `description`, `parent_group_id`, `attributes`, and `metadata`, matching the \"Common X Object\" pattern every other resource collection in this service follows.\n- `parent_group_id` supports a group hierarchy (e.g. \"Mobile Engineering\" nested under \"Engineering\"); cycles (a group becoming its own ancestor) are rejected with 400.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n1. Run the service: `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000`.\n2. Create a superuser: `uv run python scripts/create_superuser.py admin@example.com ChangeMe123!` (update `superuser_email`/`superuser_password` below if different) — needed only for Setup's organization bootstrap.\n\n**Auto token handling:** same pattern as the sibling collections — Login Test scripts capture tokens per actor into collection variables, and a collection-level pre-request script auto-refreshes a near-expired token via POST /auth/refresh before any other request runs.\n\n**Run order matters** — later folders assume earlier ones ran (Setup creates the Apple Corp tenant + owner + two department employees; folders 2-3 act on the groups created in folder 1).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level: auto-detect a near-expired/missing access token for",
          "// the current actor(s) and silently refresh it via POST /auth/refresh",
          "// before the request runs.",
          "function base64UrlDecode(input) {",
          "    input = input.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');",
          "    while (input.length % 4) { input += '='; }",
          "    return decodeURIComponent(",
          "        atob(input).split('').map(function (c) {",
          "            return '%' + ('00' + c.charCodeAt(0).toString(16)).slice(-2);",
          "        }).join('')",
          "    );",
          "}",
          "",
          "function isExpiredOrMissing(token) {",
          "    if (!token) return true;",
          "    var parts = token.split('.');",
          "    if (parts.length !== 3) return true;",
          "    try {",
          "        var payload = JSON.parse(base64UrlDecode(parts[1]));",
          "        return !payload.exp || (payload.exp * 1000) < (Date.now() + 5000);",
          "    } catch (e) {",
          "        return true;",
          "    }",
          "}",
          "",
          "function refreshActor(actor, cb) {",
          "    var accessVar = actor + '_access_token';",
          "    var refreshVar = actor + '_refresh_token';",
          "    var accessToken = pm.collectionVariables.get(accessVar);",
          "    var refreshToken = pm.collectionVariables.get(refreshVar);",
          "",
          "    if (!refreshToken || !isExpiredOrMissing(accessToken)) {",
          "        return cb();",
          "    }",
          "",
          "    pm.sendRequest({",
          "        url: pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url') + '/api/v1/auth/refresh',",
          "        method: 'POST',",
          "        header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
          "        body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ refresh_token: refreshToken }) }",
          "    }, function (err, res) {",
          "        if (!err && res && res.code === 200) {",
          "            var json = res.json();",
          "            pm.collectionVariables.set(accessVar, json.access_token);",
          "            pm.collectionVariables.set(refreshVar, json.refresh_token);",
          "            console.log('[auto-refresh] ' + actor + ' access token refreshed');",
          "        } else {",
          "            console.log('[auto-refresh] ' + actor + ' refresh skipped/failed (continuing with existing token)');",
          "        }",
          "        cb();",
          "    });",
          "}",
          "",
          "var requestName = pm.info.requestName || '';",
          "if (!/^(Login|Register|Refresh)/i.test(requestName)) {",
          "    refreshActor('superuser', function () {",
          "        refreshActor('owner', function () {",
          "            refreshActor('employee', function () {});",
          "        });",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000" },
    { "key": "superuser_email", "value": "admin@example.com" },
    { "key": "superuser_password", "value": "ChangeMe123!" },
    { "key": "superuser_access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "superuser_refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "owner_email", "value": "" },
    { "key": "owner_password", "value": "" },
    { "key": "owner_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "owner_access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "owner_refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employee_email", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employee_password", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employee_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employee_access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "employee_refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "org_slug", "value": "" },
    { "key": "organization_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "engineering_group_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "finance_group_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "child_group_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "throwaway_group_id", "value": "" }
  ],
